                SAVE AND RECALL PAGES, THE FILE CAROUSEL                       
                                                                               
The VIEWTEXT system uses a screen buffer. The page can then   
be displayed by pressing RETURN, or ESCAPE twice to return to the MAIN MENU.   
                                                                               
SAVE PAGE TO DISC - function 12 of the MAIN MENU is used split screen to display 2 pages side-by-side, with  
each page having a 40 character by 24 line format. The pages are identified as 
left (L) and right (R) in all relevant commands. The bottom line of each page  
is normally reserved for prompts and er to save pages. The    
user is prompted for a file name (as for RECALL) and the screen to be saved. If
a file already exists with that name, permission to overwrite is requested. If 
the user responds with "N", the save is abandoned and the MAIN MENU iror messages.                           
                                                                               
RECALL PAGE FROM DISC - function 11 of the MAIN MENU is used to recall any page
from disc. The user is prompted for the name of the s then    
re-displayed. If the response is "Y" the user is then prompted for an IDENT    
string, which can be up to 40 characters long. Simple editing of the string    
can be performed using the BACKSPACE key. The file is then saved, and RETURN   
wfile, which can be up to   
8 characters long in upper or lower case. If no extension is supplied (up to   
3 characters) the default extension .PGE will be used. The file name can be    
preceded by a drive code (A-H) followed by a ":" character. If noill display the page(s) or ESCAPE twice will recall the MAIN MENU. If the     
screen selected is empty, an error message is displayed.                       
                                                                               
If the file ca drive code is
supplied the drive is assumed to be the "current" drive, which will always be  
the VIEWTEXT disc.                                                             
                                                                              nnot be saved for any reason (write protected or disc full) an   
error message is displayed. Pressing RETURN will restore the MAIN MENU.        
