FILE CAROUSEL - this is a list of up to 100 file names which can be loaded by  
the PAGE, SPEED PAGE or FORMS directories. Each directory will load all file   
names on the selected drive by entering a "*" before the drive code, and will  
clear the CAROUSEL if a "*" is entered after the drive code. The number o has expired, the next 2 pages are displayed. The CAROUSEL will cycle 
back to the start of the list when all files have been displayed. Note that if 
an odd number of names are present the right page will be blank when the last  
file is displayed. Thif     
files currently held on the CAROUSEL is displayed on the front page of the     
directories, and an error message is issued if the CAROUSEL is full. As an     
example, entering "*B*" will clear and then load all filenames matching the    
direcs ensures that the order of the displayed files is the   
same for each cycle of the CAROUSEL. Files will be displayed in the order used 
when loading. The block load commands "*drive" and "*drive*" will load files   
in the order presented by the disc tory entension on disc B. "*B" will append the filenames to the CAROUSEL. 
Note that the name is held and not the file itself. When the CAROUSEL is run,  
the appropriate disc(s) MUST be currently in the drive(s) used to load the name
to the CAROUSEL. Idictionary.                                 
                                                                               
The delay can be terminated by pressing a key, and the next 2 pages will be    
displayed. If RETURN is pressed, the MAIN MENU wndividual files can be loaded by entering the drive code, and
when the file names, dates and strings have been displayed the user can enter  
"C" to select the CAROUSEL loader. The cursor will move to the first file name,
and if it is to be loaded enterill be restored at the end of  
the current display.                                                           
If a file cannot be found an error message is displayed, and pressing RETURN   
will return to the MAIN MENU.                                ing "C" will highlight the name and move the    
cursor to the next name. If not to be loaded, pressing RETURN will just move   
the cursor to the next name. Pressing ESCAPE twice will exit from the loader.  
