CAROUSEL PRINT - after the time delay has been entered, the user is prompted   
to request a print operation. If "N" is entered, the normal CAROUSEL cycle is  
performed. If "Y" is enter--
RUNNING THE CAROUSEL - function 16 of the MAIN MENU will call the CAROUSEL, and
if empty an error message is displayed. The user is prompted to enter a delay  
in seconds (127 maximum), and the first 2 pages are loaded and displayed. When 
the delayed, the delay value just entered is ignored, and the 
page(s) displayed will be printed. At the end of the print operation the MAIN  
MENU is displayed.                                                             
                                                                               
This facility in combination with the "*B*" carousel loader allows the entire  
contents of a disc to be printed with the minimum of keyboard interaction. The 
pages are printed in the order displayed.                                          (C) TANDATA   1984
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREPARING A COMMAND FILE - The command file is produced using any text editor  
which does not introduce "special" characte                           
                                                                               
                                                                               
                                                                 rs into the file (VIEWTEXT editor or
WORDSTAR in non-document mode). In most cases, the sequence of characters is   
that which would be entered via the keyboard, with the following exceptions:-  
                                                                      
                                                                               
                                                                               
                                                                                                     
ESCAPE      -      use the (!) sequence    RETURN    -    use the \ character  
